# A fight lost inside a location ends the run, the same as one lost on the road.
#
# It used to exit to the world view instead. The travel encounter was therefore the only lethal fight
# in the game: a fight picked in a location could be lost at no cost whatever, the protagonist
# walking out of it at zero health and playing on — which also made every quarrel in a location free
# to start.
#
# death_wounds.cli is the same assertion by the travel route. Both are kept: they reach TriggerDeath
# down different paths, and it was the difference between the paths that was the bug.
#
# The teardown is the second thing being tested here and cannot be seen from the death screen alone.
# Update enters its narration branch on _isInNarrativeMode rather than on the mode, so a session left
# standing would repaint itself over the death screen every frame; `expect END RUN` passing is what
# says it did not.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only brewer --save-path .tmp-cli-save/death-narration-fight.json

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

wait mode Fighting 90

fight-end death

wait mode Death 60
expect MORTAL WOUNDS
expect END RUN

expect-state savefile save none

click end-run
wait mode MainMenu 20
inspect menu
expect-state menu Continue disabled

quit
